
This illustrates a MC simulation for an ion in TIP4P water.
One can learn about the solvent structure/coordination about
the ion in this manner. The system contains the ion and 500
water molecules. Equilibration: 1M. Averaging: 2M.

Ewald sums are turned on by designating Ewald = 1 in the ionpar file.

The setup is for methylammonium ion; however,
one could use any of the Z-matrices for ions in the aazmat
directory or provide an alternative Z-matrix.

    tbucat.z       t-butyl cation
    c5h5-.z        cyclopentadienyl anion
    bnzate.z       benzoate ion
    phopo3.z       phenyl phosphate(2-) ion
    meoion.z       methoxide ion
    c186k.z        18-crown-6 K+ ion complex
    mmphos.z       methyl methylphosphonate anion
    mbphos.z       methyl benzylphosphonate anion
    mesion.z       methanethiolate ion
    tep+.z         tetraethylphosphonium ion
    tmp+.z         tetramethylphosphonium ion
    nh4ion.z       ammonium ion
    metam+.z       methylammonium ion
    phenem+.?      2-phenethylammonium ion
    acnion.z       anion of acetonitrile
    acetat.z       acetate ion
    acetf.z        fluoroacetate ion
    acetcl.z       chloroacetate ion
    sucate.z       succinate monoanion
    glyzwi.z       glycine zwitterion - 6-31G* CHELPG charges

